cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite Version 0.1.0 of this research repository."
title: "Selberg's formula as a Riccati flow, with an application to a sparse Mertens certificate"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeffery
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/selberg-riccati-flow"
url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/selberg-riccati-flow"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Wirsing showed in 1962-64 that Selberg's symmetry formula implies
  psi(x) = x + O(x/log x). This paper gives a different proof of the
  mean-square form of this bound, int_0^T t^2 f(t)^2 dt = O(T) with
  f(t) = e^{-t} psi(e^t) - 1. On each horizontal line, Selberg's formula
  becomes a Riccati equation for the normalized Laplace transform of the
  prime-power measure. Positivity at the doubled frequency keeps the
  solution away from the unstable fixed point -1, and a Mobius substitution
  makes the equation linear, giving a uniform resolvent bound. The proof
  stays in the half-plane of absolute convergence and uses no analytic
  continuation. For a general positive measure satisfying a Selberg-type
  relation, the method proves f in L^2 without a density hypothesis, which
  supplies the input for Wirsing's abstract Tauberian theorem. As an
  application, the energy bound closes a sparse divisor-cofactor
  certificate for the Mertens function, giving M(N) = O(N/log N). These
  rates are classical; the contribution is the method. The proofs were
  written and checked with AI assistance and have not been reviewed by a
  human expert.
keywords:
  - prime number theorem
  - Selberg symmetry formula
  - Riccati equation
  - Tauberian theorems
  - Mertens function
